60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a charming exercise in denial. It assumes we all inhabit identical environments, which we know is a fiction. I suspect some of us would be paying for the luxury of others' warmth.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is super simple, but @Benjamin is right—it might not feel fair if some rooms are way colder! But look at Option C! Fitting meters sounds like a total nightmare to set up and manage!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C would certainly provide the objective truth we seek, but the cost and installation process seem quite disruptive. I worry that such a clinical approach might replace our current tension with a different kind of stress.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is financially impractical. As I mentioned, the installation cost is 34,000 yen per room plus annual fees. We cannot justify such a high upfront expense when we are already struggling with budget volatility.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option C sounds like it would be a lot of work and very expensive. I'm worried that if we spend so much money and time on meters, we'll just find more things to be grumpy about.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, @Minato, I agree that Option C is a fiscal absurdity. However, Option A is a social absurdity. It rewards the lucky and punishes the shivering. I would rather we be honest about our disparities than pretend they don't exist.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, you're so focused on the shivering! But think about the work! Option A is the easiest to run, but Option B sounds like a great middle ground. It's predictable and doesn't require a huge monthly math project!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I agree that predictability brings peace. Option B could soothe the anxiety of those seasonal spikes Victoria mentioned, while avoiding the clinical coldness of individual meters. It allows us to plan our lives with a quiet mind.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, I agree. Option B addresses the volatility I found in the statements. By smoothing out the costs, we avoid the shock of those February peaks that can feel like a second rent. It is a rational compromise.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, @Jonathan, @Victoria, I like Option B too! If the amount is the same every month, we won't have to ask ""why did it change?"" and we can just be happy and friendly again!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Jonathan"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is certainly a more elegant way to handle the budget, but it is merely a financial veil. It hides the disparity of the rooms rather than solving it. Who, I wonder, will be the one shivering in February?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, you're still on about the shivering! But if we keep arguing about every single degree, we'll never stop fighting! Option B is way better because it's predictable and won't take forever to calculate every month!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, while the physical differences are real, the mental burden of constant dispute is far heavier. If we accept a predictable system, we can stop the cycle of suspicion and return to a home of quiet kindness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, we must distinguish between physical comfort and financial stability. While room differences exist, Option B prevents the budget from becoming a source of crisis. It is the only responsible way to manage our shared expenses without excessive cost.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I understand you're worried about the cold, but I'm more worried about us being mean to each other. If we stop arguing about the numbers, maybe we can just be a happy family again! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems I am the lone voice of the shivering. While Option B is a triumph of accounting, it is a failure of empathy for the drafty room. However, I shall not be the one to break our newfound harmony. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm so glad we all agree! Option B is the perfect way to keep things simple and stop the monthly math headaches. No more stress, just happiness! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a relief to see us in such harmony. By choosing predictability over precision, we protect our peace of mind and our relationships. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,Option B is the most rational choice. It provides the financial stability I seek by mitigating seasonal spikes and avoids the prohibitive costs of Option C. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we all agree! Let's stop the grumpy faces and the late payments and just be kind to each other. I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
